{{Quote|I had to get a ZX1‐capacitor from the supply depot. We have to update the D‐93 sonic tri‐denax cables. Hey, check it out. It's got a 13‐BSG‐filament enhancer and a V‐3..."<br />"Ugh, technicians.|Kazuda Xiono impersonating a First Order technician, while a [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] listens|<ref name="StS">{{Resistance|Station to Station}}</ref>}}
[[File:ConvertingShips-FO.png|thumb|right|250px|A Nautolan technician at work]]
'''Technicians''',<ref name="Letta Turmond DB">{{Databank|letta-turmond|Letta Turmond}}</ref> also known as '''mechanics''' or '''mechs''',<ref name="Harvest">{{Andor|Harvest}}</ref> were a person who was skilled in maintaining and repairing technology. [[Jackar Bowmani]] was a technician and munitions expert who worked in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] until he was [[Death|murdered]] by his wife, [[Letta Turmond]].<ref name="Letta Turmond DB" /> [[Chewbacca]] was also a skilled mechanic as he performed frequent repairs on the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' as well as reassembling the dismembered [[C-3PO]].<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref>

Certain [[droid]]s also served as expert mechanics, such as [[R2-D2]].<ref name="Databank R2-D2">{{Databank|r2-d2|R2-D2}}</ref>

[[Mich Matt]] was an [[Ishi Tib]] who worked as a technician on [[Coruscant]]'s [[central power distribution grid]].<ref name="INR">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref>

Mechanics wore durable fabric [[Clothing|coveralls]] to protect them from dirt and oil. The clothing had many pouches and pockets that held the tools that they needed for work.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

